The test does not need a Newtonian orbit. The choreography relabelling
x_i(t + T/N) = x_{i+1}(t) is KINEMATIC: it holds for N points placed at equal
time offsets along ANY closed curve, whatever the speed. Newton is needed for the
motion to be a real orbit, not for this question. So the comparison can be run on
a family of closed curves at several N, exactly and cheaply, with the true
figure-eight orbit included as a control.

CONTROL: the true figure-eight orbit, N = 3
  figure-eight (Newtonian)     N=3  e(V)= +0  2e(T)= +0  ok |  cyc(V)=[3] cyc(T^2)=[3]  NO

KINEMATIC choreographies on random closed curves
  random curve 1               N=3  e(V)= -1  2e(T)= +0  NO |  cyc(V)=[1, 2] cyc(T^2)=[3]  NO
  random curve 2               N=3  e(V)= -1  2e(T)= -4  NO |  cyc(V)=[1, 2] cyc(T^2)=[3]  NO
  random curve 3               N=3  e(V)= -1  2e(T)= +0  NO |  cyc(V)=[1, 2] cyc(T^2)=[3]  NO
